From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:46:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: DevTools, printing, Save Page As, PDF,
 Picture in Picture

Plan C15 (DevTools, View Source, PDF viewer, Picture in Picture,
printing; acceptance: the menu items of docs/arc-spec/01 work). Until
now -print and -showDevToolsWithPanel: did nothing, -savePageToURL:
failed, PDFs never loaded and requestPictureInPicture() was rejected
("not supported by the embedder").

- DevTools (openarc/browser/openarc_page_tools.mm): Chrome's bundled
  front end in an NSWindow of its own, one per tab, reused by later
  commands and closed with its tab, its close button or Cmd-W. It plays
  DevToolsWindow's part without a Browser: DevToolsUIBindings delegate
  (through a forwarding delegate the bindings own), front-end
  WebContents delegate (zoom, links open next to the inspected page,
  unhandled keys go to the app menu), panel on open (&panel=), "Inspect
  Elements" enters element-picking mode once the front end's connection
  is ready. Bridge tabs are registered as DevTools pages (previous
  patch) so every panel works.
- Printing: --disable-print-preview (print preview is a Browser-window
  tab-modal dialog) and printing::StartPrint(), i.e. the macOS print
  panel for the page, the focused frame with a selection, or the PDF
  plugin frame. window.print() shows the same panel.
- Save Page As: -savePageToURL:format: with complete page (HTML plus
  "<name>_files"), HTML only, or one MHTML file, through
  WebContents::SavePage (a download of the profile). A page that is not
  HTML (PDF, image, media) is saved as its original file, as Chrome
  does, with its own extension.
- PDF viewer: chrome.tabs resolves bridge tabs (lookup registered with
  ExtensionTabUtil, previous-but-one patch), so Chrome's OOPIF PDF
  viewer loads the document.
- Picture in Picture: the tab's WebContentsDelegate enters and leaves
  video PiP through PictureInPictureWindowManager (Chrome's floating
  window; "back to tab" reaches the shell as tabDidRequestActivation:).
  -enterPictureInPictureAutomatically: lets the shell put a playing video
  in PiP when the user leaves the tab (Arc's "Enable Picture in Picture
  when you leave a video tab"), honoring the site's auto-PiP content
  setting. Document Picture in Picture needs a Chrome window type and is
  refused up front.

Public API (OACTab.h): OACSavePageFormat, -savePageToURL:format:...,
-closeDevTools, hasPictureInPictureVideo,
-enterPictureInPictureAutomatically:, -exitPictureInPicture; -print is
printPage() in Swift.
